meta {
  name: Risk VaR - What If
  type: http
  seq: 10
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/analytics/risk/var
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "positions": [
      { "symbol": "NVDA", "quantity": 2000, "price": 500.0 },
      { "symbol": "MSFT", "quantity": -2415, "price": 414.0 }
    ],
    "confidence": 0.99,
    "horizon_days": 1.0,
    "distribution": "t"
  }
}

docs {
  Same engine against a supplied book. This particular pair is the roadmap-4.6.1 motivating case:
  a nearly-hedged long/short book where the sum-of-absolutes aggregation overstates risk several
  times over.

  "distribution": "t" switches the Monte-Carlo innovations to Student-t (rescaled to unit
  variance so only the tail fattens, not the volatility), which typically lifts 99% VaR by
  20-35% over the Gaussian.
}
